    "statement": "The function returns a result r, and r is the minimum integer x such that x ≥ n and x = 2^k - 1 for some integer k ≥ 1. Equivalently: r ≥ n; there exists an integer K ≥ 1 with r = 2^K - 1; and for every integer j ≥ 1 with 2^j - 1 ≥ n, r ≤ 2^j - 1.",
